hout the whole series  firstly there's the fact that the  participants are obviously not treated  as people but as objects they lose their  entire identity and are consistently  addressed by the mysterious operators of  the game with their participant number  in fact this already begins in the first  episode when the unknown businessman  suggests a round of the game dakshi to  gion giving him money for every round he  wins but also a slap in the face for  each time he loses this is a preliminary  test to determine whether the  participants are even susceptible to  being objectified indeed this series  conceals a lot more than mere social  criticism in the show poor is not  synonymous with good and those who are  rich are not necessarily evil the  boundaries between participants  supervisors and the frontman are vague  which is demonstrated not least by the  fact that police officer juno finds his  strongly missed brother behind the front  man's mask rather than in the morgue the  same goes for the so called vips and the  competitors many of them get into their  desperate situation through gambling  addiction and put their lives on the  line not least because of it but are the  vips so much better aren't they the ones  who bet astronomical sums on the game  players because being mere spectators  doesn't give them enough thrills a  similar symbolism concerns the two  childhood friends gil and sangwoo in the  final game they are the very ones facing  each other the two who at first sight  could not be any more different kion  seems to be the gambling addicted loser  who doesn't take care of his daughter  and still lives with his mother because  he can't afford his own apartment due to  his compulsive gambling zhong wu on the  other hand is the successful businessman  who appears to be the only one who has  made it from the bottom to the top and  is the pride and joy of his family the  longer you observe him the clearer it  becomes that he is not a whip better  than giun in fact the opposite is true  because not only does he flat out lie to  his mother he has also raised his own  gambling addiction to a much higher  level by using his company's funds so  the coin toss that takes place at the  beginning of the sixth game is actually  emblematic of the two friends they both  represent a part of the same coin at the  end when gun suggests that they both  leave the game with no price in exchange  for their lives senwoo opts to end his  life his very existence would be worth  nothing without the price and in any  case he would never have been able to  face his mother again ashamed of his own  ruthlessness after all he had been her  pride and joy  so in the end guillen wins the squid  game and does the entire competition he  is simply dumped on the street of course  not without the gigantic price of 45.6  billion won in a specially set up bank  account as well as the card that goes  with it this series eventually jumps a  year into the future and the viewer is  confronted with the reality that this  severely traumatized gion is living even  worse than he did before he has not used  any of the money in his bank account and  it appears that he would rather have  returned to his old life without money  in exchange for zang wu  thus the money is more or less an  unnecessary burden that he didn't want  in the end for the viewer this is a  rather unsatisfying ending because  although hardly anyone felt much  sympathy for the often completely  exaggerated geon one at least wished  that he would do something with the  money eventually for instance by taking  care of his daughter or the surviving  relatives of his teammates  or at the very least live a somewhat  carefree life  then out of nowhere he gets an  invitation from player 01 the friend he  actually thought was dead whom he  shamelessly deceived at first glance  during the game of marbled  the plot twist that double one is  actually the mastermind behind the games  was definitely not anticipated by many  the actually lovable and terminally ill  old man was too funny and authentic  ultimately it turns out that he  conceived the game purely for the  thrills it would give him and his vips  the only genuine thing about his faked  up story is the brain tumor that has  since confined him to bed he bets that  no one will help the dying homeless man  across the street before he freezes to  death miserably after all his premises  that all people are fundamentally  selfish  number double one dies in the course of  the encounter but more importantly the  homeless man is actually rescued by  strangers as a result guillaume is given  a wake-up call and finally sees some  meaning in his life and that is to end  the cruel games once and for all and be  in control of his own destiny with the  money he has won he ends up being seen  at the airport with a fancy suit and a  new hair color the red hair is probably  the most important symbol especially  with a possible second season in mind  throughout the series the color is green  and red have a superior meaning while  the green suits with the numbers  embroidered on them stand for the  helplessness of the participants their  color red symbolizes power not least  because all the games organizers wear  red suits throughout the show now  guillen himself wears red hair obviously  because he has become powerful however  he does not want to use his power for  cruel games instead he wants to use it  for the good for example for sebiuk's  brother whom he entrusts to the care of  seung-woo's mother along with a large  sum of money at a subway station he  eventually realizes that their games are  still taking place which is why he  henceforth makes it his mission to  avenge all the dead participants and  ruin the games  so much for the end of the first season  much more important though is the  question of what the plot might consist  of if there is to be a second season in  the following we have prepared a few  possibilities we believe could actually  happen in this or a similar way  the first and most obvious theory is  that geo will do everything in his power  to end the games he will either return  his participant to wreck the games more  or less from within or he will somehow  sneak in as a guard similar to what the  police officer did in the first season  he becomes the honorable avenger of all  those who were objective and lost their  lives perhaps in the end there will even  be a face-off between the front man and  kion this theory may seem obvious since  it would tying directly with season 1  yet the entertainment value would not be  nearly as great as it was in the first  season since you would like that new  certain something  another aspect we can think of is that  the story of the two brothers in you and  you know may not be over yet you know  ended up being shot by his brother and  falling off a cliff into the sea in most  movies this doesn't mean anything  especially when someone who's presumed  dead is suddenly out of sight it is  almost a guarantee that the person who  has miraculously survived related to  this could be the telling of the front  man's backstory how did he manage to  survive all of the games and why did he  choose to run them after winning season  2 could thus become a mix of the  frontman story and eventual alliance  between the survivor juno and kyun in  fact we consider this to be one of the  most likely scenarios not only because  series creator huang dong-hyuk has  already confirmed during an interview  with the times that he would be  interested in exploring the frontman  story in a possible second season  it is also not too far-fetched to assume  that season 2 will revolve around the  manipulator el nino his number 001 could  be emblematic of the very first squid  game which the new season could take a  closer look at we would meet the first  vips get a glimpse behind the scenes and  witness how the games are becoming  progressively more professional this  could also mean that we get to see more  violent games than in season 1 as they  have never been tested on real people  before and could therefore be even more  deadly along the way lm's story and  motivation could also be told this is  certainly not the preference of many  viewers but it is still feasible  lastly we would like to share with you  another exciting theory that is somewhat  in line with our first theory guillen  tries to end the games and eventually  becomes the front man himself in fact  this is a very classic ending for a  series like this however  it bugs us that the character  development of guillain would have to  undergo a 180 turn in order to make it  credible still there's no reason not to  assume that this is exactly what  happened with the current frontman in  home maybe he too wanted to put an end  to the entire thing but then decided to  become the frontman himself due to  various reasons the interesting part of  this theory is that there would be room  for many other theories as well so it is  possible that gion and juno team up to  stop the front man but by plot twist  goon ends up killing both the frogmen  and you know when he merges as the  overpowering leader of the games we feel  there are enough theories out there that  are far less plausible  so much for our latest original now we  are interested in your opinion are you  convinced by our theories and if so  which ones do you think are likely  perhaps you even have a hunch yourself  feel free to let us know in the comments  and if you want to see more videos like  this in the future leave us a like and  subscribe to us see you next time  [Music]  you

